1
00:00:01,871 --> 00:00:05,005
["Flower Ring" by
Shino Shimoji, Aya Suzaki plays]

2
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:34,268
[door squeaking]

3
00:01:34,398 --> 00:01:36,574
[Hiraku groaning]

4
00:01:36,705 --> 00:01:38,141
[Hiraku sighing]

5
00:01:38,272 --> 00:01:42,711
[Lu groaning]
[whimsical music]

6
00:01:42,841 --> 00:01:44,408
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
Vampires really don't

7
00:01:44,539 --> 00:01:45,931
like mornings, do they?

8
00:01:46,062 --> 00:01:47,803
But still,

9
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:49,370
having Lu living here
with me has

10
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,633
helped out in
all sorts of ways.

11
00:01:52,373 --> 00:01:55,115
[bright flute music]

12
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,508
- That should do it.

13
00:01:57,639 --> 00:01:59,206
We should be set
for lights now.

14
00:01:59,336 --> 00:02:00,163
- Wow.

15
00:02:00,294 --> 00:02:01,599
That's so amazing!

16
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:03,949
- But all I did was basic magic.

17
00:02:06,082 --> 00:02:08,693
This dish really has
a mild flavor to it.

18
00:02:08,824 --> 00:02:11,870
Do you prefer not to use salt
when cooking your meals?

19
00:02:12,001 --> 00:02:13,524
- Nope. I just don't have any.

20
00:02:13,655 --> 00:02:14,525
- Huh?

21
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:16,223
- There's no salt.

22
00:02:16,353 --> 00:02:18,660
I've been looking for awhile,
but I can't find any.

23
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:20,183
I'm at the point where
I'm about to...

24
00:02:20,314 --> 00:02:22,577
That's a pretty intense
look on your face!

25
00:02:22,707 --> 00:02:24,056
- Well, of course it is.

26
00:02:24,753 --> 00:02:25,710
Right here.

27
00:02:25,841 --> 00:02:27,234
This is mostly salt.

28
00:02:27,364 --> 00:02:29,714
We can dissolve some,
then boil it.

29
00:02:29,845 --> 00:02:32,326
Did you not notice
while you were digging?

30
00:02:32,456 --> 00:02:34,154
[Hiraku groaning]

31
00:02:34,284 --> 00:02:36,373
That's a pretty intense
look on your face.

32
00:02:37,548 --> 00:02:40,508
[Lu yawning]

33
00:02:40,638 --> 00:02:41,813
Good morning.

34
00:02:41,944 --> 00:02:42,945
- Hey.

35
00:02:43,075 --> 00:02:44,076
Good morning.

36
00:02:44,207 --> 00:02:45,687
- [Lu] What are we doing today?

37
00:02:45,817 --> 00:02:47,471
- Let me see.

38
00:02:47,602 --> 00:02:49,908
I was planning to
check on the fruit trees.

39
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,083
- Okay.

40
00:02:51,214 --> 00:02:52,563
First, I'm going to
get washed up,

41
00:02:52,694 --> 00:02:54,609
and then I'll head over there.

42
00:02:54,739 --> 00:02:55,914
[bright guitar music]

43
00:02:56,045 --> 00:02:57,089
Look at these.

44
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,048
Did you transplant them here?

45
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:00,528
- Yeah.

46
00:03:00,658 --> 00:03:03,139
They need more time to grow
than the vegetables.

47
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:06,142
I tried oranges and
peaches this time.

48
00:03:06,273 --> 00:03:08,405
I might try chestnuts next time.

49
00:03:08,536 --> 00:03:09,972
- Oh?

50
00:03:10,102 --> 00:03:12,148
I can't wait to try those
once they're harvested.

51
00:03:12,279 --> 00:03:13,802
[Lu slurping]

52
00:03:13,932 --> 00:03:15,412
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
By the way,

53
00:03:15,543 --> 00:03:18,067
the herb tea that Lu
makes is pretty good,

54
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:20,635
but I wanna drink green tea.

55
00:03:20,765 --> 00:03:22,289
If I remember correctly,

56
00:03:22,419 --> 00:03:23,768
oolong tea and black tea are

57
00:03:23,899 --> 00:03:26,336
all made from processing
the same leaves.

58
00:03:26,467 --> 00:03:27,990
[wood clanking]

59
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,819
[Hiraku gasping]
[Lu gasping]

60
00:03:30,949 --> 00:03:32,777
What is it this time?

61
00:03:32,908 --> 00:03:34,910
[suspenseful music]

62
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,564
[Hiraku panting]
[Lu panting]

63
00:03:36,694 --> 00:03:39,088
[Tia yelling]

64
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,307
- Enough!

65
00:03:40,437 --> 00:03:42,570
Please forgive my behavior!

66
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,616
I understand that I was wrong
for attacking you first!

67
00:03:45,747 --> 00:03:46,791
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I've seen this situation

68
00:03:46,922 --> 00:03:48,140
play out before.

69
00:03:48,271 --> 00:03:50,882
- Help, anyone!
Please rescue me!

70
00:03:51,013 --> 00:03:52,536
Don't let them hurt me!

71
00:03:52,667 --> 00:03:53,885
- Okay!

72
00:03:54,016 --> 00:03:55,060
[Tia sighing]

73
00:03:55,191 --> 00:03:56,714
Are you all right?

74
00:03:56,845 --> 00:03:57,715
- Yes.

75
00:03:57,846 --> 00:03:59,195
I think so.

76
00:04:01,763 --> 00:04:02,981
[Hiraku gasping]

77
00:04:04,592 --> 00:04:06,855
[magical music]

78
00:04:10,685 --> 00:04:11,425
- Wow.

79
00:04:11,555 --> 00:04:12,861
That's amazing.

80
00:04:12,991 --> 00:04:15,429
It's nice to be able
to use magic, huh?

81
00:04:15,907 --> 00:04:18,345
Lu?

82
00:04:18,475 --> 00:04:20,608
- So this is where you
were hiding out, Lulucy!

83
00:04:20,738 --> 00:04:23,437
Stop resisting and come in
quietly or I'll have to...

84
00:04:23,567 --> 00:04:25,395
[Tia yelling]

85
00:04:27,092 --> 00:04:28,137
Help me!

86
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:29,704
- [Hiraku] Hey, hey, hey!

87
00:04:29,834 --> 00:04:31,053
- [Tia] Jeez.

88
00:04:31,183 --> 00:04:32,272
I can't believe you hid

89
00:04:32,402 --> 00:04:34,143
in this forest
of all places.

90
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:36,580
- Well, a lot of stuff happened.

91
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:39,017
- That was an awful
experience back thee.

92
00:04:39,148 --> 00:04:40,149
- [Lu] I know.

93
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,803
They did that to me, too.

94
00:04:41,933 --> 00:04:43,500
- To you as well?

95
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:45,154
- Yeah. They're pretty ruthless.

96
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,721
Magic doesn't affect them much,

97
00:04:46,851 --> 00:04:48,549
plus they dodge spells.

98
00:04:48,679 --> 00:04:50,638
- [Tia] Fighting them
is a death sentence.

99
00:04:50,768 --> 00:04:52,422
- [Lu] Yeah.

100
00:04:52,553 --> 00:04:54,337
- [Hiraku Voiceover] They seem
to have a shared experience.

101
00:04:54,468 --> 00:04:56,600
- [Tia] By the way,

102
00:04:56,731 --> 00:04:58,167
who is this person?

103
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,211
- I'm Hira.

104
00:04:59,342 --> 00:05:01,431
- Oh, this person is...

105
00:05:01,562 --> 00:05:03,128
Well...

106
00:05:05,043 --> 00:05:06,697
He's my husband.

107
00:05:06,828 --> 00:05:08,133
- Your husband?

108
00:05:08,264 --> 00:05:10,266
You and Lulucy are a couple?

109
00:05:10,397 --> 00:05:11,833
- What? Yeah.

110
00:05:11,963 --> 00:05:13,574
- [Tia] I wasn't expecting that.

111
00:05:13,704 --> 00:05:15,445
- Yeah. I'm Hiraku.

112
00:05:15,576 --> 00:05:17,882
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
Her husband?

113
00:05:18,013 --> 00:05:21,408
That's the first time
she's called me that.

114
00:05:21,538 --> 00:05:23,497
- Let me introduce myself.

115
00:05:23,627 --> 00:05:25,150
My name is Tia.

116
00:05:25,281 --> 00:05:27,327
And as you can see,
I'm an angel.

117
00:05:27,457 --> 00:05:29,067
- An angel?

118
00:05:29,198 --> 00:05:32,636
So, that means
you serve God, right?

119
00:05:32,767 --> 00:05:34,377
[Tia tooting trumpet]

120
00:05:34,508 --> 00:05:36,466
- [Lu] It's nothing
that important.

121
00:05:36,597 --> 00:05:38,294
They're just
a race of warriors

122
00:05:38,425 --> 00:05:39,774
that have more muscles
than brains.

123
00:05:39,904 --> 00:05:40,818
[Tia growling]

124
00:05:40,949 --> 00:05:41,993
- [Tia] How rude!

125
00:05:42,124 --> 00:05:43,299
There was a brief
time period when

126
00:05:43,430 --> 00:05:45,040
we were an object of
worship, you know!

127
00:05:45,170 --> 00:05:48,086
- [Hiraku] So why is an angel
like you chasing down Lu?

128
00:05:48,217 --> 00:05:50,524
- There's a bounty on her for
all of the damage she caused

129
00:05:50,654 --> 00:05:52,134
from one of her rampages.

130
00:05:52,264 --> 00:05:54,136
- There's an actual
bounty on your head?

131
00:05:54,266 --> 00:05:55,398
- Well, yeah.

132
00:05:55,529 --> 00:05:56,921
There was an annoying
noble who kept

133
00:05:57,052 --> 00:05:58,619
forcing me to make medicine
and drugs for them.

134
00:05:58,749 --> 00:06:00,490
They were so incessant
with their demands

135
00:06:00,621 --> 00:06:02,231
that I felt the need
to teach them a little-

136
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:03,624
- There's nothing
little about it!

137
00:06:03,754 --> 00:06:05,103
She spends all
her time researching

138
00:06:05,234 --> 00:06:07,018
strange medicines
and concoctions,

139
00:06:07,149 --> 00:06:08,890
and then as soon as
something bothers her,

140
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:10,021
[castle exploding]

141
00:06:10,152 --> 00:06:11,458
she starts blowing
everything up.

142
00:06:11,588 --> 00:06:12,763
[Lu cartoon giggling]
That's the problem.

143
00:06:12,894 --> 00:06:14,025
- Stop making it
sound like I've

144
00:06:14,156 --> 00:06:15,244
done that multiple times!

145
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,941
There was just one accident!

146
00:06:17,072 --> 00:06:18,421
- Regardless, the fact remains

147
00:06:18,552 --> 00:06:20,292
you besmirched the honor
of a noble!

148
00:06:20,423 --> 00:06:22,033
Do you have idea...

149
00:06:22,164 --> 00:06:23,861
- [Hiraku Voiceover] They seem
to get along pretty well.

150
00:06:23,992 --> 00:06:26,647
- Well, I do think I may have
gone a little too far with that.

151
00:06:26,777 --> 00:06:29,606
- I'm surprised you're
willing to admit that.

152
00:06:29,737 --> 00:06:30,868
- So anyways,

153
00:06:30,999 --> 00:06:32,392
the reason I ended up here
is because

154
00:06:32,522 --> 00:06:33,828
I was running from Tia.

155
00:06:33,958 --> 00:06:36,700
After all, she is
stronger than I am.

156
00:06:36,831 --> 00:06:38,528
But only by a little bit.

157
00:06:38,659 --> 00:06:40,182
- Wow, Lulucy.

158
00:06:40,312 --> 00:06:42,271
I'm amazed.
You really have changed.

159
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:44,360
You never used to be
the kind of person

160
00:06:44,491 --> 00:06:46,797
who would freely admit
to having any weaknesses.

161
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:48,320
- [Lu] Yeah, well,

162
00:06:48,451 --> 00:06:50,932
I felt firsthand just
how weak I really was.

163
00:06:51,062 --> 00:06:52,499
- [Tia] I see.

164
00:06:52,629 --> 00:06:54,326
Fighting that many should
be against the rules.

165
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:55,458
- Yeah.

166
00:06:55,589 --> 00:06:57,547
Now putting that stuff aside,

167
00:06:57,678 --> 00:06:59,244
do you wanna live here, too?

168
00:06:59,375 --> 00:07:01,072
- What? Live here with you two?

169
00:07:01,203 --> 00:07:02,726
- Yes, with us.

170
00:07:02,857 --> 00:07:03,640
Right?

171
00:07:03,771 --> 00:07:05,120
- I guess.

172
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:07,731
- I'll show you around
the crop fields and stuff.

173
00:07:07,862 --> 00:07:10,081
I'm sure you'll love it here
as much as I do!

174
00:07:10,212 --> 00:07:11,866
Let's get going, okay?

175
00:07:11,996 --> 00:07:13,433
- Yeah.

176
00:07:14,738 --> 00:07:16,174
- [Lu] Look!

177
00:07:16,305 --> 00:07:18,263
[bright violin music]
These are the crop fields.

178
00:07:18,394 --> 00:07:20,222
We grow lots of vegetables here.

179
00:07:20,352 --> 00:07:21,397
- [Tia] Wow.

180
00:07:21,528 --> 00:07:23,051
- And this is our orchard.

181
00:07:23,181 --> 00:07:25,096
We have a lot of different
kinds of fruit growing.

182
00:07:25,227 --> 00:07:26,315
[Tia gasping]

183
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:30,624
This is... Zabuton!

184
00:07:30,754 --> 00:07:33,278
[Tia fainting]

185
00:07:33,409 --> 00:07:35,280
Yeah. That's about
what I expected.

186
00:07:35,411 --> 00:07:37,848
- [Hiraku] Maybe she
doesn't like spiders.

187
00:07:37,979 --> 00:07:38,936
- Hey!

188
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,329
[Tia gasping]

189
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,244
We're about to go and
harvest some crops.

190
00:07:42,374 --> 00:07:43,550
Come with us.

191
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,465
It's a whole lot of fun.

192
00:07:45,595 --> 00:07:47,075
- Kay.

193
00:07:49,207 --> 00:07:51,471
Did you plant all this
stuff yourself, Hiraku?

194
00:07:51,601 --> 00:07:52,863
- [Hiraku] Yeah.

195
00:07:52,994 --> 00:07:55,039
- [Lu] I helped a little, too.

196
00:07:55,170 --> 00:07:58,652
- We really needed some
more hands, so thank you.

197
00:07:58,782 --> 00:08:02,612
- What? You expect me to do
farm work around here, too?

198
00:08:02,743 --> 00:08:04,005
- Of course.

199
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:05,049
Come on!

200
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,268
- Why does an angel like me

201
00:08:06,398 --> 00:08:07,965
have to get their hands dirty?

202
00:08:08,096 --> 00:08:10,968
- Okay then, let's get
started with the cabbage!

203
00:08:16,365 --> 00:08:17,671
There, you see?

204
00:08:17,801 --> 00:08:20,151
Give it a try, just like that.

205
00:08:20,717 --> 00:08:22,023
- Sure.

206
00:08:23,154 --> 00:08:25,940
[Tia growling]

207
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:30,510
These are heavy cabbages, huh?

208
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,424
- Wanna taste it?

209
00:08:35,297 --> 00:08:36,733
Here.

210
00:08:36,864 --> 00:08:39,083
Well, all I did was tear up
some cabbage leaves

211
00:08:39,214 --> 00:08:40,607
and sprinkle salt.

212
00:08:44,785 --> 00:08:46,134
[Tia gasping]

213
00:08:46,264 --> 00:08:48,310
- [Tia] It's delicious! Really!

214
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,007
- I'm glad.

215
00:08:50,138 --> 00:08:53,271
- Wow, I never knew fresh
vegetables tasted so great.

216
00:08:53,402 --> 00:08:54,534
- Yeah.

217
00:08:54,664 --> 00:08:55,709
And the ones you
actually grow yourself

218
00:08:55,839 --> 00:08:57,406
taste even better.

219
00:08:57,537 --> 00:09:00,061
- I think you're right
about that.

220
00:09:01,976 --> 00:09:03,455
[Tia sighing]

221
00:09:03,586 --> 00:09:05,762
I think that's enough for today.

222
00:09:05,893 --> 00:09:07,938
- Yeah, that's a good amount.

223
00:09:08,069 --> 00:09:09,636
- That was pretty exhausting.

224
00:09:09,766 --> 00:09:11,115
- It's nice to have so much,

225
00:09:11,246 --> 00:09:13,640
but harvesting them all
is hard work.

226
00:09:16,338 --> 00:09:18,688
- Aw man, if only...

227
00:09:21,082 --> 00:09:23,127
- It's delicious!

228
00:09:23,258 --> 00:09:26,783
This red vegetable you call a
strawberry is so sweet and tart.

229
00:09:26,914 --> 00:09:28,002
- It sure is.

230
00:09:28,132 --> 00:09:29,481
- This farming work
is a lot more

231
00:09:29,612 --> 00:09:31,832
fulfilling than I ever
expected it to be.

232
00:09:31,962 --> 00:09:33,442
- [Lu] You had fun today, right?

233
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:34,574
- Yes!

234
00:09:34,704 --> 00:09:36,488
- Well, then, that settles it!

235
00:09:36,619 --> 00:09:39,317
You're going to live
here with us, right?

236
00:09:39,448 --> 00:09:40,318
- Well, I...

237
00:09:40,449 --> 00:09:42,277
- Right? Come on.

238
00:09:42,407 --> 00:09:45,062
My body won't be able to handle
everything if it's just myself.

239
00:09:45,193 --> 00:09:46,411
- [Tia] Excuse me?

240
00:09:46,542 --> 00:09:48,326
What do you mean by that?

241
00:09:48,457 --> 00:09:51,678
[bright folk music]

242
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:09,173
- Tia, I have to say,

243
00:10:09,304 --> 00:10:11,132
this farming work really
does suit you well.

244
00:10:11,262 --> 00:10:13,395
- Was that supposed to be
a compliment?

245
00:10:13,525 --> 00:10:14,483
- Of course it was.

246
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,180
- Very well, then.

247
00:10:16,311 --> 00:10:18,269
I guess we'll just have to
leave it at that for now.

248
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,619
More importantly...

249
00:10:19,749 --> 00:10:21,359
Hiraku!

250
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:24,841
Can we make a lot
more strawberries?

251
00:10:24,972 --> 00:10:26,451
- I really wish that we could,

252
00:10:26,582 --> 00:10:29,193
but even if we
expanded the crop fields,

253
00:10:29,324 --> 00:10:31,369
we couldn't keep up
with all the harvesting.

254
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,329
I think we're operating
at maximum capacity.

255
00:10:34,459 --> 00:10:35,678
[Tia sighing]

256
00:10:35,809 --> 00:10:37,114
- Yeah, we really could use

257
00:10:37,245 --> 00:10:38,594
some more help around the farm.

258
00:10:38,725 --> 00:10:40,596
- [Lu] You can just
work extra hard

259
00:10:40,727 --> 00:10:42,250
to make up the difference.

260
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:43,599
- [Tia] What about you?

261
00:10:43,730 --> 00:10:44,948
Are you sure you haven't
been slacking off?

262
00:10:45,079 --> 00:10:46,210
[Hiraku chuckling]

263
00:10:46,341 --> 00:10:47,995
- I really don't think she is.

264
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:50,475
Besides, if we grow
too much of everything,

265
00:10:50,606 --> 00:10:51,868
then it's likely
we won't be able

266
00:10:51,999 --> 00:10:54,566
to finish eating everything
that we harvest.

267
00:10:55,437 --> 00:10:58,222
[puppies whining]

268
00:10:58,353 --> 00:10:59,920
Oh, it's the new puppies.

269
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:01,878
Their horns are
already coming in.

270
00:11:02,009 --> 00:11:03,880
[Tia trembling]
[puppies whining]

271
00:11:04,011 --> 00:11:07,188
Good boy.

272
00:11:07,318 --> 00:11:12,149
Kuro and Yuki's children
had children of their own.

273
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:15,109
They've become quite a
large family of dogs.

274
00:11:15,239 --> 00:11:16,284
[Tia trembling]

275
00:11:16,414 --> 00:11:17,546
Before long,
the puppies will leave

276
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:19,287
and find partners
of their own.

277
00:11:19,417 --> 00:11:22,029
- Does that mean we'll have
even more puppies later?

278
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:23,160
[Tia yelling]

279
00:11:23,291 --> 00:11:24,640
- Now that you mention it,

280
00:11:24,771 --> 00:11:26,773
that hut isn't going to
be big enough.

281
00:11:26,903 --> 00:11:28,644
- [Hiraku Voiceover] And so,

282
00:11:28,775 --> 00:11:32,169
we decided to build a dog
area next to the orchard.

283
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,780
[Hiraku sighing]

284
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:36,260
It looks kind of like
a horse stable,

285
00:11:36,391 --> 00:11:39,263
but I'd like to think that
it turned out well.

286
00:11:39,394 --> 00:11:41,004
I still haven't
come up with names

287
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:44,312
for the next generation after
Kuroone and his siblings.

288
00:11:44,442 --> 00:11:45,966
I want to give them names,

289
00:11:46,096 --> 00:11:47,576
but there's just so many of them

290
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:50,448
that it's hard to come up
with something for everyone.

291
00:11:50,579 --> 00:11:53,930
On the other hand,
Zabuton's children...

292
00:11:55,149 --> 00:11:56,280
- [Hiraku] What is it?

293
00:12:00,763 --> 00:12:02,069
[Hiraku gasping]

294
00:12:02,199 --> 00:12:03,374
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
Are riding the wind

295
00:12:03,505 --> 00:12:05,942
and starting a new journey.

296
00:12:06,073 --> 00:12:07,465
I guess they're all leaving.

297
00:12:07,596 --> 00:12:09,641
I was planning on
turning the orchard

298
00:12:09,772 --> 00:12:11,339
into their new home.

299
00:12:11,469 --> 00:12:12,514
Oh well.

300
00:12:15,386 --> 00:12:17,780
It looks like some of them are
still staying behind with us.

301
00:12:17,911 --> 00:12:19,956
- Hey.

302
00:12:20,087 --> 00:12:22,263
I'm going to step out
for awhile, too.

303
00:12:22,393 --> 00:12:25,048
- [Hiraku] You're also going off
somewhere and leaving us?

304
00:12:25,179 --> 00:12:27,485
- No, I won't be gone
for too long, promise.

305
00:12:27,616 --> 00:12:29,357
Now then.

306
00:12:31,707 --> 00:12:33,274
- I wonder where she's going.

307
00:12:33,404 --> 00:12:35,537
- Well, she'll be back
before you know it.

308
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:36,973
- You think so?

309
00:12:37,104 --> 00:12:38,366
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
"Farming Life."

310
00:12:38,496 --> 00:12:39,497
- [Lu Voiceover]
"In Another."

311
00:12:39,628 --> 00:12:41,195
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
"World."

312
00:12:42,936 --> 00:12:44,285
A few days later,

313
00:12:44,415 --> 00:12:46,896
Tia came back just like
Lu said she would.

314
00:12:47,027 --> 00:12:50,030
And she brought
a bunch of girls with her.

315
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,466
- So you're elves?

316
00:12:51,596 --> 00:12:52,772
- We're high elves,

317
00:12:52,902 --> 00:12:54,208
but you can call us
elves if you like.

318
00:12:54,338 --> 00:12:55,992
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
What's the difference?

319
00:12:56,123 --> 00:12:58,299
- Please introduce
yourselves, everyone!

320
00:12:58,429 --> 00:12:59,430
- I'm Lea.

321
00:12:59,561 --> 00:13:00,388
- I'm Leef.

322
00:13:00,518 --> 00:13:01,432
- I'm Lecott.

323
00:13:01,563 --> 00:13:02,433
- I'm Leezay.

324
00:13:02,564 --> 00:13:03,347
- I'm Leely.

325
00:13:03,478 --> 00:13:04,392
- I'm Leeta.

326
00:13:04,522 --> 00:13:05,741
- I'm Lees.

327
00:13:05,872 --> 00:13:07,351
- [Hiraku] You're all Le.

328
00:13:07,482 --> 00:13:10,050
- Ah, you mean that
our names all have Le?

329
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:11,442
We have similar names because

330
00:13:11,573 --> 00:13:13,227
we come from the same family.

331
00:13:13,357 --> 00:13:15,272
We came here after Tia suggested

332
00:13:15,403 --> 00:13:16,796
that we all move here.

333
00:13:16,926 --> 00:13:19,189
Please let us all
live here with you!

334
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,974
- Well, um...

335
00:13:21,104 --> 00:13:22,584
- The truth is,
they all share

336
00:13:22,714 --> 00:13:24,847
a very sad and
depressing backstory.

337
00:13:24,978 --> 00:13:27,110
They all used to live
in a village

338
00:13:27,241 --> 00:13:29,460
far up into the north.

339
00:13:29,591 --> 00:13:30,897
But most of their people were

340
00:13:31,027 --> 00:13:32,550
wiped out after they got dragged

341
00:13:32,681 --> 00:13:34,291
into the war of the humans.

342
00:13:34,422 --> 00:13:36,816
Their race was scattered,
and since then,

343
00:13:36,946 --> 00:13:38,208
they've been wandering the land

344
00:13:38,339 --> 00:13:39,427
looking for a place they could

345
00:13:39,557 --> 00:13:40,994
settle down and call home.

346
00:13:41,124 --> 00:13:42,604
[Lea sighing]

347
00:13:42,734 --> 00:13:44,388
- Until now, we've been
traveling through the woods

348
00:13:44,519 --> 00:13:46,477
trying to do what we can to get
by.

349
00:13:46,608 --> 00:13:48,349
And without a place
to settle down,

350
00:13:48,479 --> 00:13:51,352
it will be impossible
to repopulate our race.

351
00:13:51,482 --> 00:13:53,093
We ask that you help us!

352
00:13:53,223 --> 00:13:54,703
- [Elves] Please help us!

353
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:57,097
- You can count on them
to be excellent workers.

354
00:13:57,227 --> 00:13:59,186
I implore you to
help them as well.

355
00:13:59,316 --> 00:14:01,188
- I think it's a good idea
for you to accept.

356
00:14:01,318 --> 00:14:03,973
I've heard the high elves
are a very talented race.

357
00:14:04,104 --> 00:14:06,758
I imagine you're all still
pretty young, right?

358
00:14:06,889 --> 00:14:08,848
- I'm the oldest one
within our group.

359
00:14:08,978 --> 00:14:10,632
I'm just over 400.

360
00:14:10,762 --> 00:14:12,677
- I'm the youngest one
in the group,

361
00:14:12,808 --> 00:14:14,549
and I'm about 300.

362
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:16,246
- [Hiraku Voiceover] I can't
tell they're 100 years apart!

363
00:14:16,377 --> 00:14:17,682
- So, what do you think?

364
00:14:17,813 --> 00:14:18,466
- Fine.

365
00:14:18,596 --> 00:14:20,076
Right, Hiraku?

366
00:14:20,207 --> 00:14:23,732
- Well, we have a lot of
different roommates here,

367
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:27,431
but if you all promise to
get along, then it's fine.

368
00:14:27,562 --> 00:14:29,520
- [Elves] Thank you
for letting us stay!

369
00:14:29,651 --> 00:14:32,654
- By the way, who are the
other roommates staying here?

370
00:14:33,829 --> 00:14:36,005
- This is Zabuton.

371
00:14:36,136 --> 00:14:38,007
[elves fainting]

372
00:14:38,138 --> 00:14:41,489
And these here...
are the dogs.

373
00:14:41,619 --> 00:14:43,883
[elves fainting]

374
00:14:44,013 --> 00:14:47,451
- [Tia] Yeah, that's about
how I expected it to go.

375
00:14:47,582 --> 00:14:48,888
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
The number of people living here

376
00:14:49,018 --> 00:14:50,150
went up suddenly,

377
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,108
so we needed a place
for them to stay.

378
00:14:52,239 --> 00:14:54,850
Lea said the seven of them
all wanted to live together,

379
00:14:54,981 --> 00:14:57,374
so we decided to build them
one big house.

380
00:14:57,505 --> 00:15:00,769
First, we started with the ditch
and the wooden fence.

381
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,423
Then, we made them
their own toilet

382
00:15:02,553 --> 00:15:04,468
and garbage disposal area.

383
00:15:08,124 --> 00:15:10,779
- That was an unbreakable tree
that's harder than steel!

384
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,781
- He cut it like nothing!

385
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,304
- [Hiraku Voiceover] When it
comes to construction,

386
00:15:14,435 --> 00:15:15,827
they know more than I do.

387
00:15:15,958 --> 00:15:18,439
And they're all
really handy, too.

388
00:15:18,569 --> 00:15:20,136
I even got to learn a lot about

389
00:15:20,267 --> 00:15:23,183
how to process lumber and
fit the logs together from them.

390
00:15:23,313 --> 00:15:25,533
I just followed their orders.

391
00:15:25,663 --> 00:15:28,014
I focused on digging holes,

392
00:15:28,144 --> 00:15:29,972
and leveling the ground,

393
00:15:30,103 --> 00:15:32,366
and gathering lumber for them.

394
00:15:32,496 --> 00:15:34,759
It took us 10 days, and then...

395
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:36,457
- It's finally done!

396
00:15:36,587 --> 00:15:37,458
- Yeah!

397
00:15:37,588 --> 00:15:39,155
- That's amazing!

398
00:15:39,286 --> 00:15:41,505
It's so much nicer than
our little hut, isn't it?

399
00:15:41,636 --> 00:15:43,159
- It really is.

400
00:15:44,378 --> 00:15:45,988
- [Hiraku Voiceover] Jealousy.

401
00:15:46,119 --> 00:15:47,598
- [Lu] Is he sulking?

402
00:15:47,729 --> 00:15:49,122
- [Tia] It looks like it.

403
00:15:49,252 --> 00:15:51,385
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
But now I've learned it,

404
00:15:51,515 --> 00:15:53,213
their technique.

405
00:15:53,343 --> 00:15:54,388
[Lu gasping]

406
00:15:54,518 --> 00:15:56,216
It might be a good idea to try

407
00:15:56,346 --> 00:15:58,435
rebuilding the little hut
we've been sleeping in.

408
00:15:58,566 --> 00:16:00,046
[elves chattering]

409
00:16:00,176 --> 00:16:01,438
The house is shaped
like a rectangle

410
00:16:01,569 --> 00:16:03,484
that stretches from
east to west.

411
00:16:03,614 --> 00:16:05,138
Just past the entranceway,

412
00:16:05,268 --> 00:16:06,356
there's a large living room that

413
00:16:06,487 --> 00:16:07,967
doubles as a dining room.

414
00:16:08,097 --> 00:16:10,186
It's a place to work
on things together,

415
00:16:10,317 --> 00:16:11,883
or where they can all eat.

416
00:16:12,014 --> 00:16:13,537
Sitting on both
the left and right

417
00:16:13,668 --> 00:16:15,800
sides of the living room
are storage rooms.

418
00:16:15,931 --> 00:16:18,107
The living room is
an open design

419
00:16:18,238 --> 00:16:20,892
that covers the first
and second floors.

420
00:16:21,023 --> 00:16:23,156
The lighting is done
with magic.

421
00:16:23,286 --> 00:16:26,942
And the second floor room sits
on top of the storage rooms.

422
00:16:27,073 --> 00:16:29,989
The second floor is where
their individual rooms are.

423
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,730
I hope that this can
become a home

424
00:16:32,861 --> 00:16:35,037
where they feel safe
and at peace.

425
00:16:39,128 --> 00:16:42,305
[elves laughing]

426
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:43,828
- It looks like they've all
gotten used to

427
00:16:43,959 --> 00:16:45,221
settling down here.

428
00:16:45,352 --> 00:16:46,701
- Yeah.

429
00:16:46,831 --> 00:16:48,746
The vegetable harvesting
seems to be going great.

430
00:16:48,877 --> 00:16:51,184
- Yeah.

431
00:16:51,314 --> 00:16:52,359
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
They're eating raw garlic

432
00:16:52,489 --> 00:16:53,621
they just picked?

433
00:16:53,751 --> 00:16:55,492
That's pretty wild.

434
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,712
- Huh?

435
00:16:57,842 --> 00:17:00,062
You use fire and
you eat meat, too?

436
00:17:00,193 --> 00:17:01,759
- Yeah, of course we do.

437
00:17:01,890 --> 00:17:03,979
- Whenever I think of elves,

438
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:06,155
I think of a race
that lives in the woods

439
00:17:06,286 --> 00:17:08,897
and is one with nature
and hates fire and stuff.

440
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,246
[Lea laughing]

441
00:17:10,377 --> 00:17:11,508
- [Lea] Where'd you get
that silly idea?

442
00:17:11,639 --> 00:17:13,206
[Lea laughing]
- Am I wrong?

443
00:17:13,336 --> 00:17:15,164
- How is anyone supposed to live

444
00:17:15,295 --> 00:17:16,861
without having the use of fire?

445
00:17:16,992 --> 00:17:19,081
- Like I said, one with nature.

446
00:17:19,212 --> 00:17:20,648
- How exactly?

447
00:17:20,778 --> 00:17:23,694
- Uh, well, you see,
you wake up with the sunrise,

448
00:17:23,825 --> 00:17:25,696
you go to sleep when it sets.

449
00:17:25,827 --> 00:17:27,394
You eat fruit from the trees.

450
00:17:27,524 --> 00:17:29,222
And you love the forest trees.

451
00:17:29,352 --> 00:17:31,746
And you refuse to wear
anything made of metal.

452
00:17:31,876 --> 00:17:34,836
- Excuse me, Hiraku.

453
00:17:34,966 --> 00:17:36,664
Don't misjudge
how harsh nature is.

454
00:17:36,794 --> 00:17:38,492
If you tried living
like that in the forest,

455
00:17:38,622 --> 00:17:40,320
you would surely die
right away.

456
00:17:40,450 --> 00:17:42,017
- I see, then.

457
00:17:42,148 --> 00:17:43,758
- Good.

458
00:17:43,888 --> 00:17:45,325
- [Hiraku Voiceover] They really
are hardcore survivalists.

459
00:17:45,455 --> 00:17:47,240
- By the way, if it's okay,

460
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:48,893
as thanks for letting us
all live here,

461
00:17:49,024 --> 00:17:50,156
we were planning on doing some

462
00:17:50,286 --> 00:17:52,158
mining and blacksmithing
work for you.

463
00:17:52,288 --> 00:17:54,029
- Huh? You can do that?

464
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,291
- [Lea] We can.

465
00:17:55,422 --> 00:17:56,945
I'd like to start by
building a furnace

466
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,381
that can melt iron.

467
00:17:58,512 --> 00:18:00,035
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I always imagined

468
00:18:00,166 --> 00:18:01,732
that dwarves handled
the blacksmithing.

469
00:18:01,863 --> 00:18:03,865
I guess that's
different in this world.

470
00:18:03,995 --> 00:18:05,084
[dwarf snoring]

471
00:18:05,214 --> 00:18:06,955
Following Lea's instruction,

472
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,913
they put together
a smithing work station.

473
00:18:09,044 --> 00:18:10,959
They put charcoal
and iron sand

474
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,265
taken from the river into the

475
00:18:12,395 --> 00:18:13,962
earthen furnace and heat it up.

476
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,747
Then they hammer the
melted iron to process it.

477
00:18:16,878 --> 00:18:17,879
[metal banging]

478
00:18:18,009 --> 00:18:19,533
[Hiraku chuckling]

479
00:18:19,663 --> 00:18:20,708
- This is amazing!

480
00:18:20,838 --> 00:18:22,275
We're advancing!

481
00:18:22,405 --> 00:18:24,277
- Thank you very much.

482
00:18:24,407 --> 00:18:26,409
- You can really do
everything, can't you?

483
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:27,628
- Well, yeah.

484
00:18:27,758 --> 00:18:29,064
That tends to happen
when you spend

485
00:18:29,195 --> 00:18:31,588
200 years wandering
without a home.

486
00:18:31,719 --> 00:18:33,068
- Oh, I'm sorry.

487
00:18:33,199 --> 00:18:36,332
- The only things
we couldn't do...

488
00:18:36,463 --> 00:18:38,726
were settle down
and finally reproduce!

489
00:18:38,856 --> 00:18:41,032
- Well, we already
took care of one of those.

490
00:18:41,163 --> 00:18:42,382
[elves giggling]

491
00:18:42,512 --> 00:18:43,687
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I thought it would be

492
00:18:43,818 --> 00:18:44,949
for the best if I
didn't say anything

493
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,299
about the second thing
she mentioned.

494
00:18:51,434 --> 00:18:53,958
- I'm really happy you guys
all came to live here.

495
00:18:54,089 --> 00:18:55,264
- Me too.

496
00:18:55,395 --> 00:18:56,396
- I'm happy to hear
that you feel

497
00:18:56,526 --> 00:18:58,049
that way about us, Hiraku.

498
00:18:58,180 --> 00:18:59,442
[leaves rustling]

499
00:18:59,573 --> 00:19:01,444
- [Hiraku] Let's stop
here for today.

500
00:19:01,575 --> 00:19:03,751
- Excuse me.

501
00:19:03,881 --> 00:19:05,231
I'm pretty sure
I saw a wheat field

502
00:19:05,361 --> 00:19:06,797
out over there,
is that right?

503
00:19:06,928 --> 00:19:08,712
- Yeah, we have
a wheat field,

504
00:19:08,843 --> 00:19:10,061
but we already processed and

505
00:19:10,192 --> 00:19:12,020
harvested it into
flour to store.

506
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,108
[Hiraku gasping]

507
00:19:13,239 --> 00:19:14,936
- If it's all right with you,

508
00:19:15,066 --> 00:19:17,286
I would like to bake
some bread for everyone.

509
00:19:17,417 --> 00:19:18,635
- Some bread?

510
00:19:18,766 --> 00:19:21,029
Yes, please, go ahead!

511
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,378
Wait, what's that?

512
00:19:22,509 --> 00:19:23,858
- If you use this stuff in here,

513
00:19:23,988 --> 00:19:26,034
it makes the bread rise up
when it bakes.

514
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:27,383
[thud]

515
00:19:27,514 --> 00:19:30,212
[bright music]

516
00:19:37,132 --> 00:19:39,395
[Leef gasping]

517
00:19:39,526 --> 00:19:41,832
[magical music]

518
00:19:41,963 --> 00:19:45,009
[Leef gasping]

519
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,708
[bread crunching]

520
00:19:47,838 --> 00:19:49,013
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
That freshly baked bread

521
00:19:49,144 --> 00:19:50,450
tasted amazing!

522
00:19:50,580 --> 00:19:52,713
[bright guitar music]

523
00:19:54,845 --> 00:19:56,238
- This is delicious!

524
00:19:56,369 --> 00:19:57,935
- [Tia] It really is!

525
00:19:58,066 --> 00:20:00,286
- We're all very happy to
hear that you enjoy it.

526
00:20:00,416 --> 00:20:02,244
- [Lu] That's an understatement.

527
00:20:02,375 --> 00:20:03,985
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
That jar must've had

528
00:20:04,115 --> 00:20:07,597
a natural yeast to make the
bread rise inside of it.

529
00:20:07,728 --> 00:20:09,077
Now that we can bake bread,

530
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,471
I'd like to expand
the wheat fields.

531
00:20:13,473 --> 00:20:15,997
- I might be late in asking,

532
00:20:16,127 --> 00:20:18,608
but does this land we're on
belong to anyone?

533
00:20:18,739 --> 00:20:20,784
- You mean like
this forest here?

534
00:20:20,915 --> 00:20:23,396
- Yeah.

535
00:20:23,526 --> 00:20:26,355
- I don't think anyone owns
this plot of land or anything,

536
00:20:26,486 --> 00:20:28,923
but I guess it's under the
control of the demon lord.

537
00:20:29,053 --> 00:20:30,185
- The demon lord?

538
00:20:30,316 --> 00:20:31,142
- Yeah.

539
00:20:31,273 --> 00:20:32,666
- That sounds terrifying.

540
00:20:32,796 --> 00:20:34,537
- Is there some sort of problem?

541
00:20:34,668 --> 00:20:37,061
- Well, it's just do you
think the demon lord

542
00:20:37,192 --> 00:20:38,759
is going to have
a problem with me

543
00:20:38,889 --> 00:20:40,761
building all these crop
fields and stuff here?

544
00:20:40,891 --> 00:20:43,329
- [Lu] Is that what
you're worried about?

545
00:20:43,459 --> 00:20:44,939
Did you receive
any kind of support

546
00:20:45,069 --> 00:20:46,984
when you started
building all this?

547
00:20:47,115 --> 00:20:48,508
- [Hiraku] No, not at all.

548
00:20:48,638 --> 00:20:51,206
- Then there's nothing
to worry about.

549
00:20:51,337 --> 00:20:53,556
If you built this place
all on your own,

550
00:20:53,687 --> 00:20:55,602
then the land belongs to you.

551
00:20:55,732 --> 00:20:57,952
- I guess that's how it works.

552
00:20:58,082 --> 00:21:00,346
- That's how it works!

553
00:21:00,476 --> 00:21:03,566
[bright folk music]

554
00:21:07,614 --> 00:21:10,791
- [Lea] Hiraku is really
full of surprises.

555
00:21:10,921 --> 00:21:13,446
- [Lu] He surprised me
a lot at first, too.

556
00:21:13,576 --> 00:21:15,012
- Not only did he tame all those

557
00:21:15,143 --> 00:21:17,493
inferno wolves by himself
without causing any harm,

558
00:21:17,624 --> 00:21:20,453
but he tamed
a demon spider, too!

559
00:21:21,410 --> 00:21:23,107
He's definitely special.

560
00:21:23,238 --> 00:21:25,109
- And all these crops as well.

561
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,329
Is the soil here
really good enough

562
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:28,852
to grow vegetables like this?

563
00:21:28,983 --> 00:21:29,984
- Who knows.

564
00:21:30,114 --> 00:21:32,029
I never got to asking him.

565
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:34,815
- I'm pretty sure he has
a very green thumb.

566
00:21:34,945 --> 00:21:36,338
[Lu sighing]

567
00:21:36,469 --> 00:21:38,558
That said, it's surprising
how lacking he is

568
00:21:38,688 --> 00:21:40,299
in knowledge about the world.

569
00:21:40,429 --> 00:21:42,431
- I know what you mean!

570
00:21:42,562 --> 00:21:43,998
He was saying that he thought

571
00:21:44,128 --> 00:21:46,479
elves were a race that
didn't use fire or eat meat,

572
00:21:46,609 --> 00:21:48,611
that we're one with nature.

573
00:21:48,742 --> 00:21:50,221
- Are you serious?

574
00:21:50,352 --> 00:21:51,745
- Not only that,

575
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:54,008
but he didn't seem to know
what angels were either.

576
00:21:54,138 --> 00:21:56,793
- That goes a few steps
beyond lacking knowledge.

577
00:21:56,924 --> 00:21:58,708
- You're right.

578
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:01,015
[bright folk music]

579
00:22:06,586 --> 00:22:08,065
- [Hiraku Voiceover] Oh yeah,

580
00:22:08,196 --> 00:22:10,154
I haven't worked on building
the waterway in awhile.

581
00:22:10,285 --> 00:22:12,809
Maybe I'll ask Lea and
the elves to help me out.

582
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:15,377
There's lots of work
to do tomorrow.

583
00:22:17,553 --> 00:22:21,035
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

584
00:23:47,687 --> 00:23:50,907
[bright folk music]

